# Type and lint checks

Before finishing any change, and again before opening a pull request, check only the Python files changed on the current branch. Do not run ruff or mypy on the whole tree.

Changed files are the committed diff against `main`, plus staged, unstaged, and untracked `*.py` files. From the repo root:

```bash
base=$(git merge-base HEAD main 2>/dev/null || git merge-base HEAD origin/main)
mapfile -t files < <(
  {
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR "$base"...HEAD
    git diff --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR HEAD
    git ls-files --others --exclude-standard
  } | grep -E '\.py$' | sort -u
)
```

If `files` is empty, skip the checks and say so. Otherwise:

```bash
uv run ruff check "${files[@]}"
uv run ruff format --check "${files[@]}"
uv run mypy --follow-imports=silent "${files[@]}"
```

Fix every failure in those files before treating the work as done or opening the pull request. Format only those files with `uv run ruff format "${files[@]}"`, then re-run the format check.
